d":"contaminant","name":"Lead"},"Surface Water Treatment Rule":{"kind":"rule","name":"Surface Water Treatment Rule","plain":"A requirement for systems drawing on surface water to filter and disinfect to a defined standard. A violation means the treatment process did not meet the required performance.","effect":null,"source":null,"who":null},"Revised Total Coliform Rule":{"plain":"Coliforms are bacteria that are mostly harmless in themselves. They are measured as an indicator: if they are present, the system may be open to something that is not harmless.","effect":"Coliforms are bacteria that are naturally present in the environment and are used as an indicator that other, potentially harmful, waterborne pathogens may be present or that a potential pathway exists through which contamination may enter the drinking water distribution system.","source":"U.S. EPA, mandatory health effects language \u2014 Revised Total Coliform Rule","who":"A warning sign rather than a harm in itself.","kind":"contaminant","name":"Revised Total Coliform Rule"}}}